Subject: [PATCH] HID: spi-hid: sequence rails and reset, manage panel and system power

Local Romulus15 test based on this machine's HSPI/GTCH ACPI and the
DRM panel-follower API used by in-tree i2c-hid. Keep rail GPIOs owned by
regulators, power down on shutdown/suspend, and rebuild HID state after
resume. Enumeration uses freezable work so children appear after thaw.

No firmware update, EC reset, or HID mode/calibration changes.
Not yet validated on hardware.

---
